# Names the AOSP list predates (brands, products, apps). Same format as en.dict: word, tab, frequency (0-255).
# Lines without a tab (like these) are ignored. Merged with en.dict at build time (:keys:buildDict).
# Only words made of letters and apostrophes (Keys ends a word at "-", "+" or "&"). Frequencies kept modest
# (60 to 90) so a name never outranks a common word as an autocorrect target. Skip names that are a one-letter
# slip from a common word (for example Ulta and "ultra", Shein and "shine"): knowing them would stop that typo being fixed.
MacBook	90
MacBooks	70
macOS	80
